1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,999
ⓘ These English & Foreign subtitles created by ZoowlCZ (ver. 2025-08) are an expanded version of the English subtitles (6053820) uploaded by lusiads to OpenSubtitles.

2
00:00:12,842 --> 00:00:25,843
{\an8} [Sindarin] ♫ <i>Estel, le iôn adar lín...</i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Hope, you are your father’s son... ♫

3
00:00:26,143 --> 00:00:35,744
{\an8} [Sindarin] ♫ <i>... û iôn naneth lín.</i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ ... not your mother’s child. ♫

4
00:00:36,214 --> 00:00:38,758
[Sindarin] <i>Anirne hene beriad i chên lîn.</i>
[English] She wanted to protect her child.

5
00:00:40,677 --> 00:00:44,472
[Sindarin] <i>Ned Imladris nauthant e le beriathar aen.</i>
[English] She thought in Rivendell you would be safe.

6
00:00:47,335 --> 00:00:50,735
In her heart, your mother knew
you'd be hunted all your life.

7
00:00:51,335 --> 00:00:53,035
That you'd never escape your fate.

8
00:00:53,535 --> 00:00:56,935
The skill of the elves can reforge
the sword of kings...

9
00:00:57,635 --> 00:01:01,335
...but only you have the power to wield it.

10
00:01:02,536 --> 00:01:04,936
I do not want that power.

11
00:01:05,236 --> 00:01:07,836
I have never wanted it.

12
00:01:09,136 --> 00:01:11,636
You are the last of that bloodline.
There is no other.

13
00:01:16,336 --> 00:01:18,537
My old sword! Sting.

14
00:01:18,937 --> 00:01:20,037
Here, take it. Take it.

15
00:01:25,437 --> 00:01:29,237
- It's so light.
- Yes, yeah. Made by the elves, you know.

16
00:01:30,037 --> 00:01:34,038
The blade glows blue when orcs are close.

17
00:01:34,538 --> 00:01:38,938
And it's times like that, my lad,
when you have to be extra careful.

18
00:01:39,238 --> 00:01:41,638
Here's a pretty thing.

19
00:01:42,138 --> 00:01:43,338
Mithril.

20
00:01:44,238 --> 00:01:48,439
As light as a feather, and as hard as dragon scales.

21
00:01:48,839 --> 00:01:51,939
Let me see you put it on. Come on.

22
00:02:00,139 --> 00:02:02,139
My old ring.

23
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:07,240
I should very much like...

24
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:11,440
...to hold it again, one last time.

25
00:02:28,941 --> 00:02:32,442
I'm sorry I brought this upon you, my boy.

26
00:02:32,942 --> 00:02:36,842
I'm sorry that you must carry this burden.

27
00:02:41,642 --> 00:02:44,542
I'm sorry for everything.

28
00:02:59,543 --> 00:03:03,744
The ring-bearer is setting out
on the quest of Mount Doom.

29
00:03:05,144 --> 00:03:07,644
On you who travel with him, no oath...

30
00:03:08,044 --> 00:03:11,044
...nor bond is laid to go further than you will.

31
00:03:14,544 --> 00:03:16,944
Farewell. Hold to your purpose.

32
00:03:17,445 --> 00:03:21,245
May the blessings of elves and men...

33
00:03:22,045 --> 00:03:24,545
...and all free folk go with you.

34
00:03:27,645 --> 00:03:31,545
The fellowship awaits the ring-bearer.

35
00:03:50,247 --> 00:03:52,647
Mordor, Gandalf, is it left or right?

36
00:03:53,247 --> 00:03:55,047
Left.

37
00:05:14,752 --> 00:05:18,853
We must hold to this course, west
of the Misty Mountains, for 40 days.

38
00:05:19,353 --> 00:05:22,853
If our luck holds, the Gap of Rohan
will still be open to us.

39
00:05:23,353 --> 00:05:26,853
From there, our road turns east to Mordor.

40
00:05:26,853 --> 00:05:30,753
Two, one, five. Good! Very good.

41
00:05:32,754 --> 00:05:33,754
Move your feet.

42
00:05:33,754 --> 00:05:35,254
- You look good, Pippin.
- Thanks.

43
00:05:35,554 --> 00:05:36,954
Faster!

44
00:05:38,254 --> 00:05:41,954
If anyone was to ask for my opinion,
which I note they're not...

45
00:05:42,254 --> 00:05:44,854
...I'd say we were taking the long way 'round.

46
00:05:45,554 --> 00:05:48,455
Gandalf.
We could pass through the mines of Moria.

47
00:05:49,155 --> 00:05:52,855
My cousin Balin would give us a royal welcome.

48
00:05:53,255 --> 00:05:58,455
No Gimli, I would not take the road through
Moria unless I had no other choice.

49
00:06:07,956 --> 00:06:09,056
Sorry!

50
00:06:09,756 --> 00:06:11,256
Get him!

51
00:06:12,756 --> 00:06:15,056
- For the Shire!
- Hold him. Hold him down, Merry!

52
00:06:15,756 --> 00:06:17,957
Gentlemen, that's enough.

53
00:06:21,857 --> 00:06:23,357
You've got my arm!
You've got my arm!

54
00:06:23,857 --> 00:06:26,457
- What is that?
- Nothing. It's just a wisp of cloud.

55
00:06:26,857 --> 00:06:29,357
It's moving fast.

56
00:06:29,757 --> 00:06:31,857
Against the wind.

57
00:06:32,658 --> 00:06:34,758
- Crebain from Dunland!
- Hide!

58
00:06:35,058 --> 00:06:37,658
- Hurry!
- Take cover!

59
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:12,860
Spies of Saruman.

60
00:07:13,660 --> 00:07:16,760
The passage south is being watched.

61
00:07:18,061 --> 00:07:21,361
We must take the pass of Caradhras.

62
00:07:33,962 --> 00:07:35,562
Frodo!

63
00:07:53,273 --> 00:08:00,383
{\an8} [Quenya] ♫ <i>I tuo, i macil...</i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ The strength, The weapon... ♫

64
00:07:54,663 --> 00:07:56,863
Boromir.

65
00:07:57,163 --> 00:08:01,363
It is a strange fate that we should
suffer so much fear and doubt...

66
00:08:00,407 --> 00:08:06,632
{\an8} [Quenya] ♫ <i>Astaldoron mauri...</i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ The needs of the valiant... ♫

67
00:08:01,363 --> 00:08:04,564
...over so small a thing.

68
00:08:06,656 --> 00:08:09,510
{\an8} [Quenya] ♫ <i>Nai túren...</i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Be it that victory... ♫

69
00:08:07,964 --> 00:08:09,864
Such a little thing.

70
00:08:10,164 --> 00:08:11,564
Boromir!

71
00:08:12,264 --> 00:08:14,764
Give the ring to Frodo.

72
00:08:24,765 --> 00:08:26,665
As you wish.

73
00:08:27,465 --> 00:08:29,465
I care not.

74
00:09:04,868 --> 00:09:09,368
So, Gandalf, you try to lead them over Caradhras.

75
00:09:09,768 --> 00:09:14,268
And if that fails, where then will you go?

76
00:09:15,768 --> 00:09:18,569
If the mountain defeats you...

77
00:09:18,869 --> 00:09:23,169
... will you risk a more dangerous road?

78
00:09:30,682 --> 00:09:34,852
[Quenya] <i>Cuiva nwalca Carnirassë!</i>
[English] Wake up cruel Redhorn!

79
00:09:35,770 --> 00:09:38,470
There is a fell voice on the air.

80
00:09:39,670 --> 00:09:41,170
It's Saruman!

81
00:09:50,171 --> 00:09:54,571
He's trying to bring down the mountain!
Gandalf, we must turn back!

82
00:09:54,971 --> 00:09:56,771
No!

83
00:09:58,881 --> 00:10:02,662
[Sindarin] <i>Losto Caradhras, Sedho! Hodo!</i>
[English] Sleep Redhorn, Be still! Lie Still!

84
00:10:03,182 --> 00:10:04,732
[Sindarin] <i>Nuitho i 'Ruith!</i>
[English] Hold your Wrath!

85
00:10:05,182 --> 00:10:10,212
[Quenya] <i>Cuiva nwalca Carnirassë!</i>
[English] Wake up cruel Redhorn!

86
00:10:10,882 --> 00:10:13,542
[Quenya] <i>Nai yarvaxëa rasselya...</i>
[English] May your bloodstained horn...

87
00:10:14,382 --> 00:10:17,683
[Quenya] <i>...taltuva ñotto-carinnar!</i>
[English] ...fall upon enemy heads!

88
00:11:03,276 --> 00:11:05,076
We must get off the mountain!

89
00:11:05,576 --> 00:11:09,776
Make for the Gap of Rohan,
and take the west road to my city!

90
00:11:10,176 --> 00:11:13,376
The Gap of Rohan takes us too close to Isengard!

91
00:11:13,676 --> 00:11:17,277
We cannot pass over a mountain.
Let us go under it.

92
00:11:17,677 --> 00:11:20,377
Let us go through the mines of Moria.

93
00:11:22,277 --> 00:11:25,877
Moria. You fear to go into those mines.

94
00:11:26,777 --> 00:11:31,577
The dwarves delved too greedily and too deep.

95
00:11:32,678 --> 00:11:37,378
You know what they awoke
in the darkness of Khazad-dûm:

96
00:11:38,778 --> 00:11:42,078
Shadow and flame.

97
00:11:45,678 --> 00:11:48,279
Let the ring-bearer decide.

98
00:11:53,079 --> 00:11:55,179
We cannot stay here!

99
00:11:55,179 --> 00:11:58,079
This will be the death of the hobbits.

100
00:11:58,379 --> 00:11:59,979
Frodo?

101
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:05,780
We will go through the mines.

102
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:08,580
So be it.

103
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:18,981
Frodo, come and help an old man.

104
00:12:22,681 --> 00:12:24,781
How is your shoulder?

105
00:12:25,081 --> 00:12:28,181
- Better than it was.
- And the ring?

106
00:12:29,881 --> 00:12:32,382
You feel its power growing, don't you?

107
00:12:32,882 --> 00:12:35,682
I've felt it too.
You must be careful now.

108
00:12:36,282 --> 00:12:39,982
Evil will be drawn to you from
outside the fellowship.

109
00:12:40,282 --> 00:12:42,782
And, I fear, from within.

110
00:12:45,582 --> 00:12:49,583
- Who then do I trust?
- You must trust yourself.

111
00:12:49,883 --> 00:12:52,583
Trust your own strengths.

112
00:12:52,983 --> 00:12:55,483
- What do you mean?
- There are many powers in this world...

113
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:57,683
...for good or for evil.

114
00:12:57,983 --> 00:13:00,183
Some are greater than I am.

115
00:13:00,783 --> 00:13:04,184
And against some I have not yet been tested.

116
00:13:05,784 --> 00:13:07,084
The walls...

117
00:13:07,884 --> 00:13:09,884
...of Moria.

118
00:13:15,684 --> 00:13:18,585
Dwarf doors are invisible when closed.

119
00:13:18,885 --> 00:13:23,085
Yes, Gimli, their own masters cannot find
them if their secrets are forgotten.

120
00:13:23,685 --> 00:13:26,085
Why doesn't that surprise me?

121
00:13:34,086 --> 00:13:37,286
Well, let's see.

122
00:13:37,686 --> 00:13:39,086
Ithildin.

123
00:13:39,786 --> 00:13:42,986
It mirrors only starlight and moonlight.

124
00:13:57,187 --> 00:14:01,587
It reads; "The Doors of Durin, Lord of Moria.

125
00:14:01,887 --> 00:14:06,588
- Speak, friend, and enter."
- What do you suppose that means?

126
00:14:06,588 --> 00:14:11,288
Oh It's quite simple. If you are a friend,
you speak the password and the doors will open.

127
00:14:11,374 --> 00:14:16,036
[Sindarin] <i>Annon Edhellen edro hi ammen!</i>
[English] Gate of the elves, open now for me!

128
00:14:23,959 --> 00:14:30,359
[Sindarin] <i>Fennas Nogothrim, lasto beth lammen.</i>
[English] Doorway of the Dwarf-folk, listen to the word of my tongue.

129
00:14:35,190 --> 00:14:36,190
Nothing's happening.

130
00:14:43,390 --> 00:14:47,391
I once knew every spell in
all the tongues of elves...

131
00:14:47,891 --> 00:14:50,591
...men and orcs.

132
00:14:50,891 --> 00:14:52,091
What are you going to do, then?

133
00:14:52,091 --> 00:14:54,491
Knock your head against these doors,
Peregrin Took!

134
00:14:54,791 --> 00:14:56,691
And if that does not shatter them...

135
00:14:56,991 --> 00:14:59,591
...and I am allowed a little
peace from foolish questions...

136
00:14:59,891 --> 00:15:03,192
...I will try to find the opening words.

137
00:15:06,402 --> 00:15:08,602
[Quenya] <i>Ando Eldarinwa...</i>
[English] Gate of elves...

138
00:15:10,102 --> 00:15:12,102
[Quenya] <i>...a lasta quettanya...</i>
[English] ...listen to my word...

139
00:15:12,902 --> 00:15:15,202
[Quenya] <i>...fenda casarinwa!</i>
[English] ...threshold of dwarves!

140
00:15:16,192 --> 00:15:18,593
Mines are no place for a pony.

141
00:15:18,993 --> 00:15:22,793
- Even one so brave as Bill.
- Bye-bye, Bill.

142
00:15:22,793 --> 00:15:24,193
Fennas Nogothrim...
(Doorway of the dwarf-folk...)

143
00:15:24,193 --> 00:15:26,893
Go on, Bill. Go on.

144
00:15:27,593 --> 00:15:31,093
Don't worry, Sam, he knows the way home.

145
00:15:37,994 --> 00:15:40,394
Do not disturb the water.

146
00:15:40,694 --> 00:15:42,594
Oh, it's useless.

147
00:15:55,295 --> 00:15:57,395
It's a riddle.

148
00:16:00,195 --> 00:16:03,296
"Speak 'friend' and enter."

149
00:16:03,796 --> 00:16:06,596
What's the elvish word for "friend"?

150
00:16:07,540 --> 00:16:08,833
[Sindarin] Mellon.
[English] Friend.

151
00:16:07,996 --> 00:16:09,296
Mellon.

152
00:16:27,397 --> 00:16:32,098
Soon, master elf, you will enjoy
the fabled hospitality of the dwarves.

153
00:16:32,698 --> 00:16:38,198
Roaring fires, malt beer, ripe meat off the bone!

154
00:16:39,998 --> 00:16:42,898
This, my friend, is the home of my cousin Balin.

155
00:16:43,498 --> 00:16:45,798
And they call it a mine.

156
00:16:45,798 --> 00:16:47,899
A mine!

157
00:16:49,099 --> 00:16:52,199
This is no mine. It's a tomb.

158
00:16:58,499 --> 00:16:59,999
No....

159
00:17:01,299 --> 00:17:02,900
No!

160
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:07,100
Goblins.

161
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:15,200
We make for the Gap of Rohan.
We should never have come here.

162
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:18,901
Now, get out of here. Get out!

163
00:17:21,801 --> 00:17:24,101
- Frodo!
- Help!

164
00:17:24,501 --> 00:17:26,001
Strider!

165
00:17:26,001 --> 00:17:28,801
- Help!
- Get off him!

166
00:17:29,101 --> 00:17:30,101
Aragorn!

167
00:17:40,602 --> 00:17:41,602
Frodo!

168
00:18:07,904 --> 00:18:09,004
Into the mines!

169
00:18:09,004 --> 00:18:12,304
- Legolas!
- Into the cave!

170
00:18:16,704 --> 00:18:18,405
Run!

171
00:18:35,406 --> 00:18:38,906
We now have but one choice.

172
00:18:39,206 --> 00:18:43,806
We must face the long dark of Moria.

173
00:18:44,306 --> 00:18:46,206
Be on your guard.

174
00:18:46,506 --> 00:18:49,807
There are older and fouler things than orcs...

175
00:18:50,207 --> 00:18:53,507
...in the deep places of the world.

176
00:19:01,607 --> 00:19:05,308
Quietly now.
It's a four-day journey to the other side.

177
00:19:05,808 --> 00:19:09,408
Let us hope that our presence may go unnoticed.

178
00:19:55,311 --> 00:19:58,911
The wealth of Moria was not in gold...

179
00:19:59,311 --> 00:20:01,611
...or jewels...

180
00:20:01,611 --> 00:20:04,812
...but mithril.

181
00:20:23,313 --> 00:20:27,913
Bilbo had a shirt of mithril rings
that Thorin gave him.

182
00:20:28,413 --> 00:20:32,214
- Oh, that was a kingly gift.
- Yes.

183
00:20:32,214 --> 00:20:34,314
I never told him...

184
00:20:34,614 --> 00:20:39,314
...but its worth was greater
than the value of the Shire.

185
00:20:51,815 --> 00:20:53,515
Pippin.

186
00:21:13,916 --> 00:21:16,716
I have no memory of this place.

187
00:21:18,917 --> 00:21:20,317
- Are we Lost?
- No.

188
00:21:20,617 --> 00:21:23,017
- I think we are.
- Gandalf's thinking.

189
00:21:23,317 --> 00:21:24,717
- Merry?
- What?

190
00:21:25,017 --> 00:21:26,817
I'm hungry.

191
00:21:38,318 --> 00:21:42,518
- There's something down there.
- It's Gollum.

192
00:21:42,918 --> 00:21:46,819
- Gollum?
- He's been following us for three days.

193
00:21:47,319 --> 00:21:51,319
- He escaped the dungeons of Barad-dûr?
- Escaped...

194
00:21:52,119 --> 00:21:53,719
...or was set loose.

195
00:21:54,319 --> 00:21:57,819
Now the ring has brought him here.

196
00:22:00,519 --> 00:22:03,220
He will never be rid of his need for it.

197
00:22:03,620 --> 00:22:09,020
He hates and loves the ring,
as he hates and loves himseIf.

198
00:22:09,420 --> 00:22:14,120
Smeagol's life is a sad story.

199
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:20,221
Yes, Smeagol he was once called.
Before the ring found him.

200
00:22:21,421 --> 00:22:24,121
Before it drove him mad.

201
00:22:24,421 --> 00:22:27,221
It's a pity Bilbo didn't kill him
when he had the chance.

202
00:22:27,521 --> 00:22:28,621
Pity?

203
00:22:29,721 --> 00:22:32,622
It is pity that stayed Bilbo's hand.

204
00:22:33,622 --> 00:22:38,622
Many that live deserve death.
Some that die deserve life.

205
00:22:40,322 --> 00:22:42,722
Can you give it to them, Frodo?

206
00:22:45,222 --> 00:22:49,023
Do not be too eager to deal
out death and judgment.

207
00:22:49,323 --> 00:22:52,123
Even the very wise cannot see all ends.

208
00:22:52,823 --> 00:22:58,523
My heart tells me that Gollum has some
part to play yet, for good or ill...

209
00:22:59,623 --> 00:23:02,324
...before this is over.

210
00:23:03,924 --> 00:23:07,624
The pity of Bilbo may rule the fate of many.

211
00:23:14,524 --> 00:23:17,725
I wish the ring had never come to me.

212
00:23:19,225 --> 00:23:21,225
I wish none of this had happened.

213
00:23:21,225 --> 00:23:26,225
So do all who live to see such times.
But that is not for them to decide.

214
00:23:27,325 --> 00:23:32,626
All we have to decide is what to do
with the time that is given to us.

215
00:23:34,326 --> 00:23:38,126
There are other forces at work in this
world, Frodo, besides the will of evil.

216
00:23:38,726 --> 00:23:41,126
Bilbo was meant to find the ring.

217
00:23:41,626 --> 00:23:45,826
In which case, you also were meant to have it.

218
00:23:46,226 --> 00:23:49,227
And that is an encouraging thought.

219
00:23:54,227 --> 00:23:56,127
It's that way.

220
00:23:56,427 --> 00:23:58,627
- He's remembered.
- No.

221
00:23:58,927 --> 00:24:02,528
But the air doesn't smell so foul down here.

222
00:24:02,828 --> 00:24:07,828
If in doubt, Meriadoc, always follow your nose.

223
00:24:22,929 --> 00:24:26,929
Let me risk a little more light.

224
00:24:31,729 --> 00:24:33,730
Behold...

225
00:24:34,230 --> 00:24:39,330
...the great realm and dwarf-city of Dwarrowdelf.

226
00:24:41,930 --> 00:24:45,230
Now there's an eye opener, and no mistake.

227
00:25:10,332 --> 00:25:12,032
Gimli!

228
00:25:19,433 --> 00:25:21,033
No!

229
00:25:23,633 --> 00:25:26,733
Oh, no.

230
00:25:28,633 --> 00:25:29,833
No.

231
00:25:37,234 --> 00:25:39,134
"Here lies Balin...

232
00:25:39,634 --> 00:25:41,634
...son of Fundin...

233
00:25:42,034 --> 00:25:44,534
...Lord of Moria."

234
00:25:45,634 --> 00:25:47,235
He is dead, then.

235
00:25:49,135 --> 00:25:50,735
It's as I feared.

236
00:26:09,036 --> 00:26:11,836
We must move on. We cannot linger.

237
00:26:12,136 --> 00:26:16,636
"They have taken the bridge and the second hall.

238
00:26:17,937 --> 00:26:20,437
We have barred the gates...

239
00:26:21,137 --> 00:26:23,537
...but cannot hold them for long.

240
00:26:23,837 --> 00:26:26,537
The ground shakes.

241
00:26:27,137 --> 00:26:28,537
Drums...

242
00:26:29,037 --> 00:26:32,238
...drums in the deep.

243
00:26:36,038 --> 00:26:37,938
We cannot get out.

244
00:26:40,038 --> 00:26:43,738
A shadow moves in the dark.

245
00:26:45,538 --> 00:26:48,039
We cannot get out.

246
00:26:51,139 --> 00:26:52,939
They are coming."

247
00:27:36,142 --> 00:27:37,942
Fool of a Took!

248
00:27:38,242 --> 00:27:41,942
Throw yourself in next time,
and rid us of your stupidity.

249
00:28:08,144 --> 00:28:09,744
Frodo!

250
00:28:12,144 --> 00:28:13,544
Orcs.

251
00:28:20,645 --> 00:28:22,545
Get back! Stay close to Gandalf!

252
00:28:29,845 --> 00:28:31,545
They have a cave-troll.

253
00:28:47,347 --> 00:28:48,547
Let them come!

254
00:28:48,947 --> 00:28:52,347
There is one dwarf yet in Moria
who still draws breath.

255
00:31:11,456 --> 00:31:14,156
I think I'm getting the hang of this.

256
00:31:18,957 --> 00:31:20,657
Frodo!

257
00:31:54,159 --> 00:31:55,959
Aragorn! Aragorn!

258
00:31:57,059 --> 00:31:58,859
Frodo!

259
00:32:44,062 --> 00:32:45,962
Frodo!

260
00:33:46,266 --> 00:33:47,567
Oh, no.

261
00:33:55,967 --> 00:33:57,767
He's alive.

262
00:34:00,367 --> 00:34:03,168
I'm all right. I'm not hurt.

263
00:34:03,468 --> 00:34:05,568
You should be dead.

264
00:34:05,968 --> 00:34:08,268
That spear would have skewered a wild boar.

265
00:34:08,568 --> 00:34:13,168
I think there's more to this
hobbit than meets the eye.

266
00:34:19,169 --> 00:34:20,269
Mithril.

267
00:34:23,069 --> 00:34:25,569
You are full of surprises, Master Baggins.

268
00:34:31,570 --> 00:34:33,370
To the bridge of Khazad-dûm!

269
00:34:48,571 --> 00:34:50,171
This way!

270
00:36:00,675 --> 00:36:03,476
What is this new devilry?

271
00:36:19,677 --> 00:36:22,477
A Balrog.

272
00:36:22,777 --> 00:36:25,877
A demon of the ancient world.

273
00:36:28,177 --> 00:36:30,477
This foe is beyond any of you.

274
00:36:31,778 --> 00:36:33,278
Run!

275
00:36:40,578 --> 00:36:42,078
Quickly!

276
00:36:58,779 --> 00:37:00,079
Gandalf.

277
00:37:00,679 --> 00:37:02,180
Lead them on, Aragorn.

278
00:37:03,680 --> 00:37:06,180
The bridge is near.

279
00:37:08,180 --> 00:37:12,180
Do as I say!
Swords are no more use here.

280
00:37:41,382 --> 00:37:43,082
Gandalf!

281
00:38:01,484 --> 00:38:02,684
Merry! Pippin!

282
00:38:13,884 --> 00:38:15,284
Sam!

283
00:38:18,085 --> 00:38:21,185
Nobody tosses a Dwarf.

284
00:38:24,385 --> 00:38:25,785
Not the beard!

285
00:38:39,086 --> 00:38:40,986
Steady.

286
00:38:42,986 --> 00:38:44,586
Hold on!

287
00:39:05,788 --> 00:39:06,988
Hang on!

288
00:39:17,689 --> 00:39:19,389
Lean forward!

289
00:39:22,489 --> 00:39:23,389
Steady.

290
00:39:24,789 --> 00:39:25,889
Come on!

291
00:39:26,189 --> 00:39:27,589
Now!

292
00:39:44,790 --> 00:39:46,491
Over the bridge!

293
00:39:46,791 --> 00:39:48,291
Fly!

294
00:40:32,994 --> 00:40:34,994
You cannot pass!

295
00:40:35,294 --> 00:40:36,894
Gandalf!

296
00:40:41,194 --> 00:40:45,894
I am a servant of the secret fire,
wielder of the flame of Anor.

297
00:40:46,995 --> 00:40:50,695
The dark fire will not avail you, flame of Udûn!

298
00:41:00,895 --> 00:41:02,796
Go back to the Shadow.

299
00:41:10,696 --> 00:41:14,896
YOU - SHALL NOT - PASS!

300
00:41:42,198 --> 00:41:45,898
- No! No!
- Gandalf!

301
00:41:53,699 --> 00:41:56,099
Fly, you fools!

302
00:42:00,299 --> 00:42:02,400
No!

303
00:42:08,600 --> 00:42:10,700
Aragorn!

304
00:43:08,204 --> 00:43:10,904
Legolas, get them up.

305
00:43:15,004 --> 00:43:16,805
Give them a moment, for pity's sake!

306
00:43:17,105 --> 00:43:20,605
By nightfall, these hills will be swarming with orcs.

307
00:43:21,005 --> 00:43:24,105
We must reach the woods of Lothlórien.

308
00:43:25,205 --> 00:43:28,405
Come, Boromir. Legolas.
Gimli, get them up.

309
00:43:30,105 --> 00:43:32,206
On your feet, Sam.

310
00:43:32,606 --> 00:43:34,006
Frodo?

311
00:43:36,106 --> 00:43:37,706
Frodo!

312
00:44:11,641 --> 00:44:22,611
{\an8} [Sindarin] ♫ <i>Man ammen toltha i dann hen morn?</i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Who brings to us this token of darkness? ♫

313
00:44:23,287 --> 00:44:33,022
{\an8} [Sindarin] ♫ <i>Si dannatha, nauva.</i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Will now fall, will be. ♫

314
00:44:30,309 --> 00:44:32,710
Stay close, young hobbits!

315
00:44:33,610 --> 00:44:37,610
They say that a great sorceress
lives in these woods.

316
00:44:34,824 --> 00:44:43,841
{\an8} [Quenya] ♫ <i>Mel~ Melma nóren sina...</i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Love for this land... ♫

317
00:44:37,910 --> 00:44:40,310
An elf-witch...

318
00:44:41,110 --> 00:44:43,810
...of terrible power.

319
00:44:44,510 --> 00:44:46,611
All who look upon her...

320
00:44:45,059 --> 00:44:54,078
{\an8} [Quenya] ♫ <i>...núra ala eäro núr.</i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ ...greater than sea deeps. ♫

321
00:44:46,611 --> 00:44:48,611
...fall under her spell.

322
00:44:48,911 --> 00:44:50,111
<i>Frodo!</i>

323
00:44:52,411 --> 00:44:54,411
And are never seen again.

324
00:44:54,411 --> 00:44:58,911
<i>Your coming to us is as the footsteps of doom.</i>

325
00:44:59,311 --> 00:45:02,912
<i>You bring great evil here, ring-bearer.</i>

326
00:45:03,312 --> 00:45:04,912
Mr. Frodo?

327
00:45:10,412 --> 00:45:15,812
Well, here's one dwarf she won't ensnare so easily.

328
00:45:16,112 --> 00:45:20,513
I have the eyes of a hawk and the ears of a fox.

329
00:45:28,313 --> 00:45:32,714
The dwarf breathes so loud, we
could have shot him in the dark.

330
00:45:36,960 --> 00:45:40,262
[Sindarin] <i>Mae govannen, Legolas Thranduilion.</i>
[English] Welcome, Legolas son of Thranduil.

331
00:45:40,637 --> 00:45:43,765
[Sindarin] <i>Govannas vîn gwennen le, Haldir o Lórien.</i>
[English] Our fellowship stands in your debt, Haldir of Lórien.

332
00:45:46,024 --> 00:45:48,124
[Sindarin] <i>A Aragorn in Dúnedain...</i>
[English] Oh, Aragorn of the Dúnedain...

333
00:45:48,425 --> 00:45:50,225
[Sindarin] <i>...istannen le ammen.</i>
[English] ...you are known to us.

334
00:45:50,715 --> 00:45:51,515
Haldir.

335
00:45:51,515 --> 00:45:53,215
So much for the legendary courtesy of the elves!

336
00:45:53,515 --> 00:45:55,415
Speak words we can all understand!

337
00:45:55,415 --> 00:46:00,015
We have not had dealings with
the dwarves since the dark days.

338
00:46:00,415 --> 00:46:02,816
And you know what this dwarf says to that?

339
00:46:03,216 --> 00:46:07,816
Ishkhaqwi ai durugnul!
(I spit upon your grave!)

340
00:46:09,816 --> 00:46:11,716
That was not so courteous.

341
00:46:18,317 --> 00:46:22,217
You bring great evil with you.

342
00:46:24,217 --> 00:46:26,317
You can go no further.

343
00:46:31,928 --> 00:46:34,698
[Sindarin] <i>Boe ammen veriad lîn. Andelu i ven!</i>
[English] We need your protection. The road is too dangerous!

344
00:46:37,728 --> 00:46:39,128
[Sindarin] <i>Merin le telim.</i>
[English] I wish we may come with you.

345
00:46:40,328 --> 00:46:42,028
[Sindarin] <i>Boe ammen i dulu lîn!</i>
[English] We need your support!

346
00:46:43,218 --> 00:46:46,018
Aragorn!

347
00:46:56,429 --> 00:46:58,029
[Sindarin] <i>Merin le telim.</i>
[English] I wish we may come with you.

348
00:47:00,769 --> 00:47:02,370
[Sindarin] <i>Andelu i ven!</i>
[English] The road is too dangerous!

349
00:47:03,720 --> 00:47:06,220
Gandalf's death was not in vain.

350
00:47:07,520 --> 00:47:09,320
Nor would he have you give up hope.

351
00:47:10,920 --> 00:47:14,120
You carry a heavy burden, Frodo.

352
00:47:15,220 --> 00:47:18,221
Don't carry the weight of the dead.

353
00:47:21,121 --> 00:47:23,121
You will follow me.

354
00:47:34,922 --> 00:47:36,822
Caras Galadhon.

355
00:47:37,422 --> 00:47:40,322
The heart of Elvendom on earth.

356
00:47:40,322 --> 00:47:46,022
Realm of the Lord Celeborn
and of Galadriel, Lady of Light.

357
00:47:46,304 --> 00:47:57,504
{\an8} [Quenya] ♫ <i>Ela i cá</i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Behold the light! ♫

358
00:47:57,733 --> 00:48:09,134
{\an8} [Quenya] ♫ <i>Nenya sina...</i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Nenya is this... ♫

359
00:48:09,154 --> 00:48:25,655
{\an8} [Quenya] ♫ <i>...corma úhátima...</i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ ...ring unbreakable... ♫

360
00:48:25,735 --> 00:48:40,436
{\an8} [Quenya] ♫ <i>...i haryanye.</i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ ...that I possess. ♫

361
00:49:05,428 --> 00:49:08,328
The enemy knows you have entered here.

362
00:49:09,128 --> 00:49:14,028
What hope you had in secrecy is now gone.

363
00:49:16,028 --> 00:49:20,229
Eight there are here, yet nine there
were set out from Rivendell.

364
00:49:20,729 --> 00:49:22,529
Tell me, where is Gandalf?

365
00:49:22,529 --> 00:49:25,729
For I much desire to speak with him.

366
00:49:26,029 --> 00:49:28,629
I can no longer see him from afar.

367
00:49:29,729 --> 00:49:34,630
Gandalf the Grey did not pass
the borders of this land.

368
00:49:35,130 --> 00:49:37,430
He has fallen into shadow.

369
00:49:42,230 --> 00:49:46,531
He was taken by both shadow and flame.

370
00:49:48,431 --> 00:49:51,931
A Balrog of Morgoth.

371
00:49:52,831 --> 00:49:56,131
For we went needlessly into the net of Moria.

372
00:49:58,331 --> 00:50:01,432
Needless were none of the deeds of Gandalf in life.

373
00:50:02,232 --> 00:50:05,432
We do not yet know his full purpose.

374
00:50:10,232 --> 00:50:14,332
Do not let the great emptiness
of Khazad-dûm fill your heart...

375
00:50:14,732 --> 00:50:16,933
...Gimli, son of Gloin.

376
00:50:18,033 --> 00:50:21,433
For the world has grown full of peril...

377
00:50:23,033 --> 00:50:25,633
...and in all lands...

378
00:50:25,933 --> 00:50:29,333
...love is now mingled with grief.

379
00:50:42,034 --> 00:50:44,734
What now becomes of this fellowship?

380
00:50:45,434 --> 00:50:48,235
Without Gandalf, hope is lost.

381
00:50:51,335 --> 00:50:54,535
The quest stands upon the edge of a knife.

382
00:50:54,535 --> 00:50:57,635
Stray but a little and it will fail...

383
00:50:58,635 --> 00:51:01,336
...to the ruin of all.

384
00:51:05,836 --> 00:51:11,336
Yet hope remains while the company is true.

385
00:51:13,136 --> 00:51:17,637
Do not let your hearts be troubled.
Go now and rest...

386
00:51:18,237 --> 00:51:21,837
...for you are weary with sorrow and much toil.

387
00:51:24,237 --> 00:51:26,237
Tonight, you will sleep....

388
00:51:26,637 --> 00:51:29,937
<i>Welcome, Frodo of the Shire...</i>

389
00:51:31,538 --> 00:51:33,238
<i>...one who has seen the eye!</i>

390
00:51:34,648 --> 00:51:39,048
{\an8} [Sindarin chorus] ♫ <i> In gwidh ristennin... </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ The bonds cut... ♫

391
00:51:39,048 --> 00:51:45,448
{\an8} [Quenya solo] ♫ <i> Ilfirin nairelma. </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Undying is our regret. ♫

392
00:51:45,449 --> 00:51:54,150
{\an8} [Sindarin chorus] ♫ <i> ...i fae narchannen. </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ ...the spirit broken. ♫

393
00:51:47,939 --> 00:51:50,439
A lament for Gandalf.

394
00:51:54,151 --> 00:51:57,455
{\an8} [Quenya solo] ♫ <i> Nauva i nauva. </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ What should be shall be. ♫

395
00:51:57,456 --> 00:52:05,645
{\an8} [Sindarin chorus] ♫ <i> I Lach Anor ed...  </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ The Flame of Anor out... ♫

396
00:51:57,839 --> 00:51:59,239
What do they say about him?

397
00:51:59,739 --> 00:52:02,140
I have not the heart to tell you.

398
00:52:05,140 --> 00:52:07,340
For me, the grief is still too near.

399
00:52:05,645 --> 00:52:13,662
{\an8} [Quenya solo] ♫ <i> Ilfirin nairelma... </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Undying is our regret... ♫

400
00:52:10,340 --> 00:52:13,140
I bet they don't mention his fireworks.

401
00:52:13,540 --> 00:52:16,341
There should be a verse about them.

402
00:52:13,662 --> 00:52:18,367
{\an8} [Sindarin chorus] ♫ <i> ...ardhon gwannen.  </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ ...left this world. ♫

403
00:52:18,367 --> 00:52:22,405
{\an8} [Quenya solo] ♫ <i> ...ar ullume nucuvalme. </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ ...yet we will cast all away. ♫

404
00:52:19,841 --> 00:52:21,741
The finest rockets ever seen

405
00:52:22,406 --> 00:52:35,185
{\an8} [Sindarin chorus] ♫ <i> Mithrandir, a Randir Vithren... </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Mithrandir, o Pilgrim Grey... ♫

406
00:52:22,941 --> 00:52:25,741
They burst in stars of blue and green

407
00:52:26,841 --> 00:52:31,842
Or after thunder, silver showers

408
00:52:32,642 --> 00:52:35,342
Came falling like a rain of flowers

409
00:52:35,209 --> 00:52:42,976
{\an8} [Sindarin chorus] ♫ <i> ...ú-reniathach... </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ ...you will not journey... ♫

410
00:52:35,742 --> 00:52:39,442
Oh, that doesn't do them justice by a long road.

411
00:52:42,977 --> 00:52:47,273
{\an8} [Quenya solo] ♫ <i> Nauva i nauva. </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ What should be shall be. ♫

412
00:52:47,273 --> 00:52:53,196
{\an8} [Sindarin chorus] ♫ <i> ...i amar galen. </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ ...the world green. ♫

413
00:52:50,343 --> 00:52:52,943
Take some rest.

414
00:52:53,196 --> 00:52:59,803
{\an8} [Quenya solo] ♫ <i> Melme nóren sina... </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Love for this land... ♫

415
00:52:53,243 --> 00:52:55,843
These borders are well-protected.

416
00:52:56,143 --> 00:52:58,543
I will find no rest here.

417
00:52:59,804 --> 00:53:12,925
{\an8} [Sindarin chorus] ♫ <i> I reniad lín ne môr nuithannen. </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ The journey of you in darkness stopped. ♫

418
00:53:01,544 --> 00:53:04,344
I heard her voice inside my head.

419
00:53:04,844 --> 00:53:08,344
She spoke of my father and the fall of Gondor.

420
00:53:08,644 --> 00:53:13,844
She said to me; "Even now there is hope Left."

421
00:53:12,925 --> 00:53:20,225
{\an8} [Quenya solo] ♫ <i> Ilfirin nairelma... </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Undying is our regret... ♫

422
00:53:15,544 --> 00:53:18,145
But I cannot see it.

423
00:53:19,645 --> 00:53:22,045
It is long since we had any hope.

424
00:53:20,225 --> 00:53:28,225
{\an8} [Quenya solo] ♫ <i> ...ar ullume nucuvalme. </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ ...yet we will cast all away. ♫

425
00:53:32,346 --> 00:53:34,446
My father is a noble man.

426
00:53:35,246 --> 00:53:37,446
But his rule is failing...

427
00:53:40,646 --> 00:53:43,046
...and our people lose faith.

428
00:53:44,646 --> 00:53:48,047
He looks to me to make things right,
and I would do it.

429
00:53:48,347 --> 00:53:51,747
I would see the glory of Gondor restored.

430
00:53:54,747 --> 00:53:57,647
Have you ever seen it, Aragorn?

431
00:53:58,347 --> 00:54:00,247
The white tower of Ecthelion.

432
00:54:00,647 --> 00:54:04,248
Glimmering like a spike of pearl and silver.

433
00:54:05,048 --> 00:54:08,448
Its banners caught high in the morning breeze.

434
00:54:11,548 --> 00:54:13,448
Have you ever been called home...

435
00:54:13,448 --> 00:54:17,449
...by the clear ringing of silver trumpets?

436
00:54:18,249 --> 00:54:21,249
I have seen the white city...

437
00:54:21,749 --> 00:54:23,149
...long ago.

438
00:54:24,249 --> 00:54:29,049
One day, our paths will lead us there.

439
00:54:30,149 --> 00:54:32,950
And the tower guard shall take up the call:

440
00:54:33,650 --> 00:54:36,750
"The Lords of Gondor have returned."

441
00:55:44,154 --> 00:55:46,555
Will you look into the mirror?

442
00:55:46,855 --> 00:55:48,255
What will I see?

443
00:55:51,355 --> 00:55:53,655
Even the wisest cannot tell.

444
00:55:54,555 --> 00:55:56,355
For the mirror...

445
00:55:56,655 --> 00:55:59,055
...shows many things.

446
00:56:02,156 --> 00:56:04,356
Things that were...

447
00:56:04,756 --> 00:56:07,256
...things that are...

448
00:56:08,056 --> 00:56:09,856
...and some things...

449
00:56:13,656 --> 00:56:16,857
...that have not yet come to pass.

450
00:57:39,462 --> 00:57:42,262
I know what it is you saw.

451
00:57:44,762 --> 00:57:47,063
For it is also in my mind.

452
00:57:49,063 --> 00:57:52,863
<i>It is what will come to pass if you should fail.</i>

453
00:57:55,463 --> 00:58:00,063
<i>The fellowship is breaking.
It is already begun.</i>

454
00:58:00,964 --> 00:58:04,164
<i>He will try to take the ring.</i>

455
00:58:04,464 --> 00:58:06,364
<i>You know of whom I speak.</i>

456
00:58:07,464 --> 00:58:11,864
<i>One by one, it will destroy them all.</i>

457
00:58:13,664 --> 00:58:15,965
<i>If you ask it of me...</i>

458
00:58:16,465 --> 00:58:19,365
<i>... I will give you the one ring.</i>

459
00:58:20,665 --> 00:58:22,765
<i>You offer it to me freely.</i>

460
00:58:27,265 --> 00:58:31,066
<i>I do not deny that my heart
has greatly desired this.</i>

461
00:58:37,766 --> 00:58:40,866
In place of a dark lord, you would have a queen...

462
00:58:41,366 --> 00:58:44,966
...not dark but beautiful and terrible as the dawn!

463
00:58:45,866 --> 00:58:48,767
Treacherous as the sea!

464
00:58:49,267 --> 00:58:54,067
Stronger than the foundations of the earth!

465
00:58:54,767 --> 00:58:57,067
All shall love me...

466
00:58:57,367 --> 00:59:00,067
...and despair.

467
00:59:14,268 --> 00:59:18,469
I pass the test. I will diminish...

468
00:59:18,869 --> 00:59:21,169
...and go into the West...

469
00:59:21,569 --> 00:59:25,869
...and remain Galadriel.
- I cannot do this alone.

470
00:59:29,569 --> 00:59:33,570
You are a ring-bearer, Frodo.
To bear a ring of power...

471
00:59:34,670 --> 00:59:36,070
...is to be alone.

472
00:59:39,570 --> 00:59:42,270
This is Nenya, the ring of Adamant.

473
00:59:42,570 --> 00:59:44,070
And I am its keeper.

474
00:59:47,371 --> 00:59:50,871
This task was appointed to you.

475
00:59:52,071 --> 00:59:54,771
And if you do not find a way...

476
00:59:56,171 --> 00:59:58,071
...no one will.

477
00:59:58,571 --> 01:00:01,572
Then I know what I must do.

478
01:00:02,272 --> 01:00:03,472
It's just...

479
01:00:06,772 --> 01:00:08,972
...I'm afraid to do it.

480
01:00:12,472 --> 01:00:17,473
Even the smallest person can change
the course of the future.

481
01:00:23,073 --> 01:00:28,573
Do you know how the orcs first came into being?

482
01:00:29,573 --> 01:00:32,674
They were elves once.

483
01:00:33,974 --> 01:00:37,174
Taken by the dark powers...

484
01:00:37,674 --> 01:00:40,674
...tortured and mutilated.

485
01:00:41,074 --> 01:00:46,175
A ruined and terrible form of life.

486
01:00:46,575 --> 01:00:48,375
And now...

487
01:00:49,975 --> 01:00:51,775
...perfected.

488
01:00:52,575 --> 01:00:55,575
My fighting Uruk-hai...

489
01:00:57,675 --> 01:00:59,875
...whom do you serve?

490
01:01:00,175 --> 01:01:02,576
Saruman!

491
01:01:23,477 --> 01:01:26,777
Hunt them down. Do not stop until, they are found.

492
01:01:27,177 --> 01:01:29,977
You do not know pain.
You do not know fear.

493
01:01:30,277 --> 01:01:33,078
You will taste man-flesh!

494
01:01:38,278 --> 01:01:41,778
One of the halflings carries
something of great value.

495
01:01:42,178 --> 01:01:46,179
Bring them to me alive and unspoiled.

496
01:01:48,279 --> 01:01:49,479
Kill the others.

497
01:02:00,956 --> 01:02:14,877
{\an8} [Quenya] ♫ <i> Ai! Laurië lantar lassi súrinen. </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Alas! Like gold fall leaves in the wind. ♫

498
01:02:08,680 --> 01:02:13,880
Never before have we clad strangers
in the garb of our own people.

499
01:02:15,180 --> 01:02:18,881
May these cloaks help shield
you from unfriendly eyes.

500
01:02:26,181 --> 01:02:27,781
Lembas.

501
01:02:28,081 --> 01:02:29,681
Elvish waybread.

502
01:02:32,082 --> 01:02:34,982
One small bite is enough to fill
the stomach of a grown man.

503
01:02:41,582 --> 01:02:43,482
How many did you eat?

504
01:02:43,482 --> 01:02:45,282
Four.

505
01:02:51,183 --> 01:02:53,683
Every league you travel south,
the danger will increase.

506
01:02:53,983 --> 01:02:57,883
Mordor orcs now hold the
eastern shore of the Anduin.

507
01:02:58,283 --> 01:03:00,683
Nor will you find safety on the western bank.

508
01:03:00,984 --> 01:03:04,684
Strange creatures bearing the mark of the
white hand have been seen on our borders.

509
01:03:05,084 --> 01:03:09,884
Seldom do orcs journey in the open
under the sun, yet these have done so.

510
01:03:18,315 --> 01:03:20,459
[Sindarin] <i>Le aphadar aen.</i>
[English] You are being tracked.

511
01:03:22,785 --> 01:03:27,185
By river you have the chance of outrunning
the enemy to the falls of Rauros.

512
01:03:44,686 --> 01:03:49,287
<i>My gift for you, Legolas, is a bow of the Galadhrim.</i>

513
01:03:49,687 --> 01:03:52,987
<i>Worthy of the skill of our woodland kin.</i>

514
01:03:58,587 --> 01:04:00,988
<i>These are the daggers of the Noldorin.</i>

515
01:04:01,288 --> 01:04:05,088
<i>They have already seen service in war.</i>

516
01:04:05,388 --> 01:04:07,588
<i>Do not fear, young Peregrin Took.</i>

517
01:04:07,888 --> 01:04:10,988
<i>You will find your courage.</i>

518
01:04:12,988 --> 01:04:14,988
<i>And for you, Samwise Gamgee...</i>

519
01:04:14,988 --> 01:04:17,889
<i>...Elven rope made of hithlain.</i>

520
01:04:17,889 --> 01:04:20,089
Thank you, my lady.

521
01:04:21,989 --> 01:04:25,189
Have you run out of those nice, shiny daggers?

522
01:04:31,690 --> 01:04:34,590
And what gift would a dwarf ask of the elves?

523
01:04:34,990 --> 01:04:37,090
Nothing.

524
01:04:37,790 --> 01:04:40,990
Except to look upon the lady
of the Galadhrim one last time...

525
01:04:41,690 --> 01:04:46,691
...for she is more fair than all
the jewels beneath the earth.

526
01:04:53,891 --> 01:04:55,391
Actually....

527
01:04:55,691 --> 01:04:57,291
There was one thing.

528
01:04:58,191 --> 01:05:00,691
No, no, I couldn't.
It's quite impossible.

529
01:05:00,992 --> 01:05:03,692
Stupid to ask.

530
01:05:06,392 --> 01:05:08,392
<i>I have nothing greater to give...</i>

531
01:05:08,392 --> 01:05:12,092
<i>...than the gift you already bear.</i>

532
01:05:12,795 --> 01:05:13,838
[Sindarin] <i>Am meleth dîn...</i>
[English] For her love...

533
01:05:15,114 --> 01:05:20,370
[Sindarin] <i>...I ant e guil Arwen Undómiel pígatha.</i>
[English] ...the gift of life of Arwen will fade.

534
01:05:21,521 --> 01:05:23,358
[Sindarin] <i>Aníron i e broniatha...</i>
[English] I wish that she endures...

535
01:05:24,084 --> 01:05:28,404
[Sindarin] <i>...Ad ae periatham athar i methid en-amar hen.</i>
[English] ...even if we separate beyond the limits of this world.

536
01:05:31,107 --> 01:05:37,120
[Sindarin] <i>Aníron i e círatha na Valinor.</i>
[English] I wish that she sails to Valinor.

537
01:05:37,594 --> 01:05:40,494
That choice is yet before her.

538
01:05:41,394 --> 01:05:44,194
You have your own choice to make, Aragorn.

539
01:05:44,594 --> 01:05:50,095
To rise above the height of all your
fathers since the days of Elendil...

540
01:05:50,595 --> 01:05:54,795
...or to fall into darkness
with all that is left of your kin.

541
01:06:01,881 --> 01:06:02,916
[Quenya] <i>Namárië.</i>
[English] Farewell.

542
01:06:07,195 --> 01:06:10,073
[Sindarin] <i>Nadath nâ i moe cerich...</i>
[English] There is much you have yet to do...

543
01:06:12,580 --> 01:06:13,873
[Sindarin] <i>...dan...</i>
[English] ...but...

544
01:06:16,857 --> 01:06:20,017
[Sindarin] <i>...ú-'eveditham, Elessar.</i>
[English] ...we shall not meet again, Elessar.

545
01:06:22,597 --> 01:06:25,697
<i>Farewell, Frodo Baggins.</i>

546
01:06:25,697 --> 01:06:29,197
<i>I give you the light of Earendil...</i>

547
01:06:30,197 --> 01:06:32,398
<i>...our most beloved star.</i>

548
01:06:41,598 --> 01:06:45,799
<i>May it be a light for you in dark places...</i>

549
01:06:46,199 --> 01:06:50,199
<i>... when all other lights go out.</i>

550
01:06:59,299 --> 01:07:02,300
I have taken my worst wound at this parting...

551
01:07:03,100 --> 01:07:07,100
...having looked my last upon that which is fairest.

552
01:07:08,100 --> 01:07:11,300
Henceforth I will call nothing fair
unless it be her gift to me.

553
01:07:11,700 --> 01:07:13,600
What was her gift?

554
01:07:13,900 --> 01:07:18,601
I asked her for one hair from her golden head.

555
01:07:19,501 --> 01:07:22,301
She gave me three.

556
01:09:04,608 --> 01:09:07,908
Gollum. He has tracked us since Moria.

557
01:09:11,808 --> 01:09:14,708
I had hoped we would lose him on the river.

558
01:09:15,108 --> 01:09:18,109
But he's too clever a waterman.

559
01:09:19,109 --> 01:09:22,309
And if he alerts the enemy to our whereabouts...

560
01:09:22,309 --> 01:09:24,609
...it will make the crossing even more dangerous.

561
01:09:24,909 --> 01:09:26,909
Have some food, Mr. Frodo.

562
01:09:27,209 --> 01:09:30,209
- No, Sam.
- You haven't eaten anything all day.

563
01:09:30,609 --> 01:09:33,510
You're not sleeping, neither.
Don't think I haven't noticed.

564
01:09:34,510 --> 01:09:37,410
- Mr. Frodo
- I'm all right.

565
01:09:37,710 --> 01:09:38,810
But you're not.

566
01:09:39,210 --> 01:09:41,710
I'm here to help you.

567
01:09:41,710 --> 01:09:43,510
I promised Gandalf that I would.

568
01:09:49,611 --> 01:09:52,111
You can't help me, Sam.

569
01:09:54,511 --> 01:09:56,111
Not this time.

570
01:09:59,111 --> 01:10:01,112
Get some sleep.

571
01:10:07,512 --> 01:10:09,612
Minas Tirith is the safer road.

572
01:10:10,212 --> 01:10:12,812
You know that.
From there we can regroup.

573
01:10:13,612 --> 01:10:15,713
Strike out for Mordor from a place of strength.

574
01:10:16,113 --> 01:10:18,813
There is no strength in Gondor that can avail us.

575
01:10:19,513 --> 01:10:21,413
You were quick enough to trust the elves.

576
01:10:23,313 --> 01:10:26,113
Have you so little faith in your own people?

577
01:10:26,113 --> 01:10:29,113
Yes, there is weakness.
There is frailty.

578
01:10:29,513 --> 01:10:32,714
But there is courage also,
and honor to be found in men.

579
01:10:33,014 --> 01:10:35,114
But you will not see that.

580
01:10:35,614 --> 01:10:36,914
You are afraid!

581
01:10:37,314 --> 01:10:39,714
All your life, you have hidden in the shadows.

582
01:10:40,114 --> 01:10:43,414
Scared of who you are, of what you are.

583
01:10:46,015 --> 01:10:50,215
I will not lead the ring within
a hundred leagues of your city.

584
01:11:02,216 --> 01:11:03,516
Frodo.

585
01:11:05,416 --> 01:11:06,816
The Argonath.

586
01:11:07,069 --> 01:11:23,862
{\an8} [Quenya] ♫ <i> Et Eärello, Endorenna utúlien. </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ Out of the Great Sea, to Middle-earth I am come. ♫

587
01:11:10,416 --> 01:11:13,916
Long have I desired to look upon the kings of old.

588
01:11:14,816 --> 01:11:16,617
My kin.

589
01:11:23,863 --> 01:11:34,140
{\an8} [Quenya] ♫ <i> Sinome, maruvan, ar hildinyar. </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ In this place, I will abide, and my heirs. ♫

590
01:12:35,822 --> 01:12:37,822
We cross the lake at nightfall.

591
01:12:38,222 --> 01:12:40,622
Hide the boats and continue on foot.

592
01:12:40,922 --> 01:12:44,222
- We approach Mordor from the North.
- Oh, yes?

593
01:12:44,822 --> 01:12:48,523
Just a simple matter of finding
our way through Emyn Muil...

594
01:12:48,823 --> 01:12:51,923
...an impassable labyrinth of razor-sharp rocks.

595
01:12:52,223 --> 01:12:55,223
And after that, it gets even better.

596
01:12:55,723 --> 01:13:00,423
Festering, stinking marshland
as far as the eye can see.

597
01:13:00,924 --> 01:13:02,224
That is our road.

598
01:13:03,824 --> 01:13:06,924
I suggest you take some rest and
recover your strength, Master Dwarf.

599
01:13:07,224 --> 01:13:08,824
Recover my...

600
01:13:12,024 --> 01:13:13,824
- We should Leave now.
- No.

601
01:13:14,124 --> 01:13:18,325
Orcs patrol the eastern shore.
We must wait for cover of darkness.

602
01:13:18,725 --> 01:13:22,125
It is not the eastern shore that worries me.

603
01:13:22,425 --> 01:13:26,225
A shadow and a threat has
been growing in my mind.

604
01:13:26,925 --> 01:13:30,926
Something draws near.
I can feel it.

605
01:13:33,126 --> 01:13:37,826
Recover strength?
Pay no heed to that, young hobbit.

606
01:13:38,626 --> 01:13:40,226
Where's Frodo?

607
01:14:05,928 --> 01:14:07,828
None of us should wander alone.

608
01:14:09,128 --> 01:14:11,228
You, least of all.

609
01:14:11,528 --> 01:14:13,828
So much depends on you.

610
01:14:15,028 --> 01:14:16,929
Frodo?

611
01:14:24,129 --> 01:14:26,629
I know why you seek solitude.

612
01:14:27,429 --> 01:14:30,730
You suffer. I see it day by day.

613
01:14:31,630 --> 01:14:34,630
You sure you do not suffer needlessly?

614
01:14:36,330 --> 01:14:38,930
There are other ways, Frodo.

615
01:14:39,230 --> 01:14:42,930
- Other paths that we might take.
- I know what you would say.

616
01:14:43,230 --> 01:14:46,831
It would seem like wisdom but
for the warning in my heart.

617
01:14:47,231 --> 01:14:50,231
Warning...against what?

618
01:14:50,531 --> 01:14:52,531
We're all afraid, Frodo.

619
01:14:52,831 --> 01:14:56,331
But to let that fear drive us,
to destroy what hope we have...

620
01:14:56,731 --> 01:15:00,331
...don't you see that is madness?
- There is no other way.

621
01:15:02,332 --> 01:15:05,432
I ask only for the strength to defend my people!

622
01:15:07,232 --> 01:15:09,132
- If you would but lend me the ring.
- No.

623
01:15:10,432 --> 01:15:13,932
- Why do you recoil? I am no thief.
- You are not yourself.

624
01:15:16,033 --> 01:15:19,133
What chance do you think you have?

625
01:15:19,433 --> 01:15:23,933
They will find you.
They will take the ring.

626
01:15:24,333 --> 01:15:27,933
And you will beg for death before the end!

627
01:15:30,233 --> 01:15:32,234
You fool!

628
01:15:32,234 --> 01:15:36,334
It is not yours, save by unhappy chance!
It could have been mine.

629
01:15:36,634 --> 01:15:39,334
It should be mine! Give it to me!

630
01:15:39,634 --> 01:15:40,834
- Give it to me!
- No!

631
01:15:41,134 --> 01:15:42,934
- Give it to me!
- No.

632
01:15:50,635 --> 01:15:52,535
I see your mind.

633
01:15:52,935 --> 01:15:55,735
You will take the ring to Sauron!

634
01:15:56,035 --> 01:15:57,835
You will betray us!

635
01:15:58,135 --> 01:16:01,236
You'll go to your death, and the death of us all!

636
01:16:01,736 --> 01:16:05,236
Curse you!
Curse you and all the halflings!

637
01:16:12,436 --> 01:16:13,936
Frodo?

638
01:16:18,237 --> 01:16:19,837
Frodo.

639
01:16:23,837 --> 01:16:25,737
What have I done?

640
01:16:26,037 --> 01:16:27,737
Please, Frodo.

641
01:16:28,037 --> 01:16:30,538
Frodo, I'm sorry!

642
01:16:57,024 --> 01:16:59,024
[Black Speech] Akha...
[English] Here...

643
01:17:00,349 --> 01:17:02,150
[Black Speech] ...ashi...
[English] ...only...

644
01:17:00,940 --> 01:17:04,440
Ash Ghurûm
(They will fall)

645
01:17:02,211 --> 01:17:03,711
[Black Speech] ...gurum!
[English] ...death!

646
01:17:19,241 --> 01:17:20,541
Frodo?

647
01:17:21,841 --> 01:17:24,841
- It has taken Boromir.
- Where is the ring?

648
01:17:25,241 --> 01:17:26,941
Stay away!

649
01:17:27,341 --> 01:17:28,941
Frodo!

650
01:17:31,242 --> 01:17:34,942
- I swore to protect you.
- Can you protect me from yourself?

651
01:17:37,427 --> 01:17:42,490
{\an8} [Quenya] ♫ <i> I tuo, i macil. </i> ♫
{\an8} [English] ♫ The strength, The weapon. ♫

652
01:17:44,842 --> 01:17:47,143
Would you destroy it?

653
01:17:52,343 --> 01:17:54,143
<i>Aragorn.</i>

654
01:17:57,643 --> 01:17:59,843
<i>Aragorn.</i>

655
01:18:01,844 --> 01:18:03,544
<i>Elessar.</i>

656
01:18:11,244 --> 01:18:14,444
I would have gone with you to the end.

657
01:18:15,244 --> 01:18:18,045
Into the very fires of Mordor.

658
01:18:21,545 --> 01:18:22,645
I know.

659
01:18:25,045 --> 01:18:30,345
Look after the others. Especially Sam.
He will not understand.

660
01:18:34,346 --> 01:18:35,946
Go, Frodo!

661
01:18:39,046 --> 01:18:40,546
Run.

662
01:18:40,546 --> 01:18:42,346
Run!

663
01:19:06,948 --> 01:19:08,548
Mr. Frodo!

664
01:19:18,049 --> 01:19:19,649
Find the halfling!

665
01:19:21,349 --> 01:19:23,749
Find the halfling!

666
01:19:27,449 --> 01:19:29,049
Elendil!

667
01:19:35,550 --> 01:19:37,050
Aragorn, go!

668
01:19:58,751 --> 01:20:00,051
Frodo!

669
01:20:00,652 --> 01:20:02,252
Hide here. Quick!

670
01:20:02,952 --> 01:20:04,352
Come on!

671
01:20:06,852 --> 01:20:08,852
What's he doing?

672
01:20:13,052 --> 01:20:15,052
He's leaving.

673
01:20:19,953 --> 01:20:22,753
- No!
- Pippin!

674
01:20:27,753 --> 01:20:29,953
Run, Frodo. Go!

675
01:20:30,654 --> 01:20:33,554
- Hey! Hey, you!
- Over here!

676
01:20:34,154 --> 01:20:35,654
- Over here!
- This way!

677
01:20:46,655 --> 01:20:48,855
- It's working!
- I know it's working! Run!

678
01:21:44,258 --> 01:21:47,159
- The horn of Gondor.
- Boromir.

679
01:22:30,462 --> 01:22:31,462
Run!

680
01:26:03,176 --> 01:26:04,676
No.

681
01:26:08,776 --> 01:26:11,676
- They took the little ones.
- Hold still.

682
01:26:11,976 --> 01:26:13,976
Frodo. Where is Frodo?

683
01:26:15,977 --> 01:26:17,377
I let Frodo go.

684
01:26:18,077 --> 01:26:20,577
Then you did what I could not.

685
01:26:21,677 --> 01:26:24,877
I tried to take the ring from him.

686
01:26:25,477 --> 01:26:29,577
- The ring is beyond our reach now.
- Forgive me.

687
01:26:29,977 --> 01:26:32,178
I did not see it.

688
01:26:32,478 --> 01:26:35,578
- I have failed you all.
- No, Boromir.

689
01:26:36,178 --> 01:26:38,578
You fought bravely.

690
01:26:38,978 --> 01:26:41,478
You have kept your honor.

691
01:26:42,278 --> 01:26:43,978
Leave it.

692
01:26:44,478 --> 01:26:46,479
It is over.

693
01:26:47,779 --> 01:26:52,879
The world of men will fall and
all will come to darkness...

694
01:26:53,479 --> 01:26:56,279
...and my city to ruin.

695
01:27:00,480 --> 01:27:03,180
I do not know what strength is in my blood...

696
01:27:03,180 --> 01:27:07,280
...but I swear to you, I will
not let the white city fall...

697
01:27:08,380 --> 01:27:10,780
...nor our people fail.

698
01:27:11,780 --> 01:27:13,180
Our people.

699
01:27:17,081 --> 01:27:19,081
Our people.

700
01:27:40,882 --> 01:27:43,782
I would have followed you, my brother.

701
01:27:45,483 --> 01:27:47,383
My captain.

702
01:27:50,183 --> 01:27:51,983
My king.

703
01:28:11,684 --> 01:28:13,784
Be at peace...

704
01:28:14,384 --> 01:28:16,185
...son of Gondor.

705
01:28:32,686 --> 01:28:35,886
They will look for his coming from the white tower.

706
01:28:36,586 --> 01:28:39,486
But he will not return.

707
01:29:02,888 --> 01:29:04,788
Frodo!

708
01:29:24,289 --> 01:29:27,489
<i>I wish the ring had never come to me.</i>

709
01:29:28,789 --> 01:29:31,590
<i>I wish none of this had happened.</i>

710
01:29:34,790 --> 01:29:37,490
<i>So do all who live to see such times...</i>

711
01:29:37,790 --> 01:29:41,090
<i>...but that is not for them to decide.</i>

712
01:29:41,490 --> 01:29:43,990
<i>All you have to decide...</i>

713
01:29:44,290 --> 01:29:48,891
<i>...is what to do with the time that is given to you.</i>

714
01:30:17,793 --> 01:30:19,793
Frodo, no!

715
01:30:20,593 --> 01:30:21,793
Frodo!

716
01:30:22,493 --> 01:30:25,093
- Mr. Frodo!
- No, Sam.

717
01:30:28,793 --> 01:30:30,694
Go back, Sam!

718
01:30:31,294 --> 01:30:34,694
- I'm going to Mordor alone.
- Of course you are.

719
01:30:34,994 --> 01:30:37,694
And I'm coming with you!

720
01:30:38,394 --> 01:30:40,694
You can't swim!

721
01:30:44,494 --> 01:30:46,195
Sam!

722
01:30:51,795 --> 01:30:53,195
Sam!

723
01:31:34,098 --> 01:31:36,798
I made a promise, Mr. Frodo.

724
01:31:37,198 --> 01:31:41,298
A promise:
"Don't you leave him, Samwise Gamgee."

725
01:31:42,598 --> 01:31:45,099
And I don't mean to.

726
01:31:45,499 --> 01:31:47,599
I don't mean to.

727
01:31:49,399 --> 01:31:51,099
Oh Sam.

728
01:32:06,100 --> 01:32:07,700
Come on.

729
01:32:36,102 --> 01:32:40,502
Hurry! Frodo and Sam have
reached the eastern shore.

730
01:32:55,603 --> 01:33:00,504
- You mean not to follow them.
- Frodo's fate is no longer in our hands.

731
01:33:04,004 --> 01:33:08,704
Then it has all been in vain.
The fellowship has failed.

732
01:33:20,705 --> 01:33:23,805
Not if we hold true to each other.

733
01:33:25,305 --> 01:33:29,605
We will not abandon Merry and
Pippin to torment and death.

734
01:33:30,706 --> 01:33:35,806
Not while we have strength left.
Leave all that can be spared behind.

735
01:33:37,306 --> 01:33:39,206
We travel light.

736
01:33:39,506 --> 01:33:41,406
Let us hunt some orc.

737
01:33:44,406 --> 01:33:46,407
Yes!

738
01:34:05,408 --> 01:34:06,808
Mordor.

739
01:34:07,508 --> 01:34:10,708
I hope the others find a safer road.

740
01:34:11,808 --> 01:34:14,308
Strider will look after them.

741
01:34:15,409 --> 01:34:18,609
I don't suppose we'll ever see them again.

742
01:34:19,109 --> 01:34:21,409
We may yet, Mr. Frodo.

743
01:34:21,409 --> 01:34:23,109
We may.

744
01:34:25,309 --> 01:34:26,409
Sam...

745
01:34:30,010 --> 01:34:32,510
...I'm glad you are with me.

